This README file contains a brief description of the verification case.

A simple test for a 1mm x 1mm x 1mm case with only 1 element. The temperature rise from 
673.15 K at 0 s till 1673.15 K at 50s. The thermal strain as well as the displacement are
outputed to verify if they were well coded. 

BAF = 1.0 - total isotropic thermal expansion
BAF != 1.0 - Orthotropic thermal expansion. The thermal expansion coef along x direction differ 
             from that of y and z direction.  




